# pacman installs the binary; what an earlier ai-session left in your home is
# yours to move, and the first run does most of it.
post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
==> kizuna was ai-session, a command called `ai`. If you used it:
    - the first run moves ~/.config/ai to ~/.config/kizuna and leaves a link
      at the old path for sessions an older ai is still running;
    - a source build in $(go env GOPATH)/bin (kizuna, or ai) comes before
      /usr/bin on most PATHs: remove it, or it shadows this package;
    - then re-point the hooks and MCP servers at this binary:
        kizuna integrate messaging <profile>
MSG
}
